---
/**
 * Home: dateline, hero (kicker + headline on cols 1–8, portrait plate on 9–12),
 * the introduction with its first paragraph as a lede, "§ 01 · Recent writing"
 * as four ledger rows, closing on "All notes →".
 * The introduction text is carried verbatim from the Hugo home (hugo.toml).
 */
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import profile from '../assets/profile.jpg';
import NoteCardStatic from '../components/NoteCardStatic.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
import { readingTime } from '../scripts/format';

const recent = (await getCollection('notes', ({ data }) => !data.draft))
  .sort((a, b) => b.data.date.getTime() - a.data.date.getTime())
  .slice(0, 4);
---

<Base title={SITE.homeTitle} description={SITE.description}>
  <p class="dateline">{SITE.dateline}</p>

  <section class="hero home-hero" aria-labelledby="hero-headline" data-hero-stage>
    <div class="hero-text">
      <span class="kicker" data-load-reveal style="--i: 0">Sam Lamrabte · Political economist &amp; analyst</span>
      <h1 id="hero-headline" class="hero-headline" data-load-reveal style="--i: 1">
        Observing the world through a political economy lens: <em>Where regulation, technology, and markets meet.</em>
      </h1>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-aside" data-load-reveal style="--i: 2">
      <figure class="plate hero-plate">
        <Picture
          class="no-dim"
          src={profile}
          alt="Sam Lamrabte"
          formats={['avif']}
          fallbackFormat="webp"
          width={1008}
          widths={[336, 672, 1008]}
          sizes="(max-width: 63.9375rem) 320px, 25vw"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="intro" aria-label="Introduction">
    <p class="lede" data-load-reveal style="--i: 3">
      My name is Sam Lamrabte. I'm a young political economist and analyst interested in the macroeconomy,
      geopolitics, financial markets, and the regulation shaping all three.
    </p>
    <div class="prose intro-prose" data-reveal>
      <p>
        This site is an introduction to who I am, and a record of what I'm reading, building, and working on. I tend
        to spend my time reading about a topic, organising what I've read into notes, or playing with ideas and models
        I'm trying to build — so a slightly more formal way of documenting that felt useful (perhaps for my own benefit
        and retention as much as anything else).
      </p>
      <p>My <a href="/cv/">CV</a> provides the detail about my experience, interests, and accomplishments.</p>
      <p>
        The TLDR version: having gotten a taste for a range of problems through my studies in Amsterdam and my work
        across international relations, public policy, research, and the private sector, I realised I couldn't look
        past economics as my core interest. I kept circling the same question — how complex regulation and
        political-economic forces actually shape the way institutions (and we) behave. Taking that seriously, I knew I
        needed more training, and began with a minor in Economic Analysis in New York at the Bert W. Wasserman
        Department of Economics and Finance (Zicklin School of Business, Baruch College, CUNY). The programme had a
        heavy quantitative finance component, and the hours spent modelling asset returns stuck with me. Being in NYC,
        surrounded by a more market-oriented educational culture, fortified my grasp of applied economics, but it also
        sharpened my desire to get back to Europe, where I started my path and where systematic research and
        structural analysis (and critique) are central. My Master's in Political Economy in Amsterdam let me examine
        the field through several lenses at once: public policy, AI and data governance, computational and qualitative
        research methods, and international regulatory systems.
      </p>
      <p>
        The end result is that I'm building a career at the intersection of economics, politics, markets, and the
        digital world drawing on both qualitative research and quantitative modelling. I'm interested in roles where
        rigorous thinking and an appetite for complexity actually count; whether in research, strategy, policy, or
        finance. In the meantime, I'm seeking any opportunity to keep thinking, writing, and modelling in this space,
        and to keep sharpening the technical toolkit alongside it (the CFA being one current step).
      </p>
      <p>
        Thanks for visiting, and if any part of this strikes a chord with you, please <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>reach out</a>!
      </p>
    </div>
    <p class="intro-cv" data-reveal><a class="ui-link" href="/cv/">→ Read the CV</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="recent-writing">
    <h2 id="recent-writing" class="section-head">§ 01 · Recent writing</h2>
    <ul class="rows" data-reveal-group>
      {
        recent.map((note) => (
          <NoteCardStatic
            slug={note.id}
            title={note.data.title}
            summary={note.data.summary}
            date={note.data.date}
            tags={note.data.tags}
            readingTime={readingTime(note.body ?? '', 230)}
          />
        ))
      }
    </ul>
    <p class="section-foot" data-reveal><a class="ui-link" href="/notes/">All notes →</a></p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  /* The hero sits 2rem under the dateline; the plate starts level with the kicker. */
  .home-hero { padding-top: var(--space-8); }
  .home-hero .hero-plate { margin-top: 0; border: 0; }
  /* The headline keeps the first edition's serif and its italic phrase. */
  .hero-headline { font-family: var(--font-headline); font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: -0.015em; }
  .hero-headline em { font-style: italic; }

  .intro { margin-top: var(--space-16); }
  .intro .lede { max-width: var(--measure-wide); }
  .intro-prose { margin-top: var(--space-8); }
  .intro-cv { margin: var(--space-8) 0 0; }

  .section-foot { margin: var(--space-6) 0 0; }

  @media (max-width: 63.9375rem) {
    .home-hero .hero-plate { margin-top: 0; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 47.9375rem) {
    .intro { margin-top: var(--space-12); }
  }
</style>
